    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0337" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 [Merchant, Livingston T.]: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edgar</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-05T17:00:00+09:00">May 5, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 6—4:22 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>143. From Merchant. Taipei’s 141 and 142, May 4 raise basic policy recommendation
                    arrived at in isolation and to consideration of which I believe Parker, with his
                    knowledge Formosan economy, and I could contribute. Despite no reply Taipei’s
                    114, April 12, I again recommend with added sense its importance that we both be
                    recalled for consultation Washington. Though Treasury has instructed Parker to
                    proceed to his post Cairo direct by June 1, I believe that at request
                    Department, <pb facs="0338" n="328" xml:id="pg328"/> this travel via Washington
                    would be authorized for above purpose. [Merchant.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edgar</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
